.TH CHTTPSVR_SET_ENGINE_LOGGER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_set_engine_logger \- set the logger for engine-level diagnostics
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_set_engine_logger(clog cl);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Derives a child logger from cl and adds the field
component=http-server-engine to it.  It then installs that child
logger as the diagnostics logger of the shared reactor.  It closes the
logger that an earlier call derived, and the fallback logger of a
running engine, when there is one.

The reactor logs to this handle at exactly three points: a TLS
handshake failure, a listen-socket bind failure, and each pass of the
idle-timeout sweep that closes one or more connections.  The engine
installs a fallback logger automatically when no logger from this
function is in place as the engine starts.  That fallback logger
writes to fd 2 at level CLOG_FATAL, the same way as the internal
stderr-only and FATAL-only logger of ccol_create_chttpsvr.  All three
diagnostic points above log below CLOG_FATAL, so the min_level of that
fallback logger filters every one of them out.  The fallback logger is
therefore silent in practice.  Use this function to install a logger
that says more.

You can call this function at any time.  This includes before the
first chttpsvr_start, while the reactor already runs, and after a full
engine stop.  The child logger serves the reactor that runs now, if
one does, and every reactor that a later chttpsvr_start brings up after
a full engine stop, until another call of this function replaces it.

cl must not be CLOG_INVALID.  The library owns the derived child
logger.  It closes it when another call replaces it, and at the exit
of the process or the unload of the library when no engine runs then.
The caller must not close it.  The caller keeps ownership of
cl and may close cl at any time: the child logger is a handle of its
own, and it keeps the destination of cl open as long as it lives.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success on success.
ccol_invalid_args when cl is CLOG_INVALID.
ccol_not_enough_memory when the library cannot allocate the child
                  logger.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_start (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_stop (3),
.BR chttpsvr_engine_wait (3)
